Quoth Topi Linkala in the annals of <cpb41v$51i$1@nyytiset.pp.htv.fi> ...
> Benjamin Lewis wrote:
> 
> > On the other hand, having items mysteriously appear out of thin air
> > whenever a monster dies bothers me, and goes beyond my suspension of
> > disbelief, especially since there are no particularly convincing
> > game-enhancing reasons to do so.  Why can't monsters' inventory be
> > generated with the monster, instead of when the monster dies?

That's also my problem with it.
> 
> For rationale of death drop I've suggested that it represents those 
> items that the monsters have but do not remember to use. This is the 
> same effect which the players confront when after DYWYPI they realize 
> that they had a wand of teleportation or some such that would have 
> prevented the DYWYPI in the first place, but they did not remember that 
> hey were carrying it.

This doesn't explain why *you* don't see these items with a wand of probing, 
and you can't steal them as a nymph or with a bullwhip.
> 
> These could be generated when the monster is generated but in this case 
> they should be marked so that the monster never uses the item. Unless we 
> do this we'll starting to find kobolds having wands of death or some such.

So what's wrong with that? It would be extremely rare. Besides, not all 
monsters know how to use every type of item; that in itself would prevent 
every scary item automatically being used against you.
> 
> The reason for death drop is that it's the only way of introducing 
> totaly random items into a dungeon in which all levels have already been 
> created. Unless we satisfy this condition some other way (like 
> restocking shops) we cannot abolish death drop as it would mean more 
> games that cannot be finished.
> 
> Today the only way to screw up the game is by converting before quest. 
> If there is no way to generate new random items then a well timed BoH 
> accident would mean a no-win game. Do you want this??
> 
Non-parallel examples. The only way to absolutely prevent ascension is to 
convert before the quest; plenty of other mistakes are lethal an extremely 
high percentage of the time. On the other hand, how many BoH accidents that 
late into the game actually prevent ascension? Everything you *absolutely* 
need won't go into the bag.

Anyway, I agree that generation of new random items is a Positive Thing. 
Death drop is just a bad kludge to accomplish it. Randomly generated 
monsters could be generated with more randomly generated stuff. Shops could 
in fact be slowly restocked. And levels reentered after a long period of 
time could have more stuff randomly distributed; this should be accompanied 
by monsters being moved around and a chance that any stashes would be 
disturbed (your stuff would be in monster's inventories).

In other words, I think the idea that "nothing happens on a level while 
you're not on it" is ridiculous.

